<%# Shared right-side navbar user section.

    Slot locals (all optional). Each slot names a partial to render in
    that position — a String partial path, or a Hash of
    { partial: "path", locals: { ... } } when the partial needs locals:
      balance_slot     — balance display, rendered at the start of the
                         top row (e.g. a wallet balance link)
      extra_icons_slot — app-specific icon buttons, rendered before the
                         admin gear + theme toggle
      div2_slot        — replaces the default second row (the wallet
                         address + level progress bar) entirely
                         (e.g. a seeds bar)

    Other locals:
      show_logout_link — boolean, show explicit "Log out" link in the
                         second row (Studio uses this)

    Legacy string locals (deprecated): balance_html, extra_icons_html,
    div2_html — pre-rendered HTML injected via raw. Still honored when
    the matching slot local is absent, so existing call sites render
    unchanged. Prefer the slot locals for new work; they go through the
    normal partial pipeline instead of trusting a raw string.
%>
<% balance_slot     ||= nil %>
<% extra_icons_slot ||= nil %>
<% div2_slot        ||= nil %>
<% balance_html     ||= nil %>
<% extra_icons_html ||= nil %>
<% show_logout_link ||= false %>
<% div2_html        ||= nil %>
<%# Slot resolution: the slot local wins when both a slot and its legacy
    string are passed. Returns nil when neither is present. %>
<% studio_nav_slot = lambda do |slot, legacy_html|
     if slot.is_a?(Hash)
       render slot[:partial], **slot.fetch(:locals, {})
     elsif slot.present?
       render slot.to_s
     elsif legacy_html.present?
       raw legacy_html
     end
   end %>

<%# Where the account link (the username and the avatar, one link) points.

    A HOST'S OWN account_path WINS: an app that already has an account page keeps
    it rather than being repointed at a thinner /profile by a routine dependency
    bump. An app adopting /profile flips over by DELETING its account route, so
    the last step of the migration is the deliberate one.

    NO CONSUMER EXERCISES THAT BRANCH TODAY, and the comment here said otherwise
    until 2026-08-14. turf-monster is the only app with an account_path, and it
    ships its own app/views/components/_user_nav.html.erb — a host view SHADOWS
    the engine's in this non-isolated engine, so turf never renders THIS file.
    The rule is for apps that adopt /profile later.

    nil when NEITHER exists, and then the name and avatar render as plain text.
    They used to render `href="#"`, which was not a graceful degradation but a
    dead link. Who that actually reached: mcritchie-industries and
    acquisition-studio — the consumers rendering this partial rather than a fork
    of it. A link that goes nowhere looks identical to one that works until it is
    clicked, which is why nobody reported it.
%>
<% studio_nav_destination =
     if defined?(account_path)
       account_path
     elsif defined?(profile_path)
       profile_path
     end %>

<div class="flex gap-2">
  <% if logged_in? %>
    <%# Left column: Div 1 + Div 2 stacked.
        flex-1 WITHOUT min-w-0: this column holds the icons, which must never
        be squeezed, so it keeps min-width auto (its min-content, the icon row)
        and the account link beside it is what gives way — the name truncates
        inside the link. The level row's text is absolutely positioned, so it
        adds nothing to that min-content. %>
    <div class="flex-1">
      <%# Div 1 (Bigger): balance + icons. %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 leading-none" :style="'padding: 0 6px;' + ($store.devMode ? 'background: cornflowerblue;' : '')">
        <%= studio_nav_slot.call(balance_slot, balance_html) %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-auto self-end">
          <%= studio_nav_slot.call(extra_icons_slot, extra_icons_html) %>
          <%# Skipped when the link sidebar carries the admin menu — two cog
              glyphs side by side read as a double gear. %>
          <%= render "components/admin_dropdown" unless respond_to?(:studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu?) && studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu? %>
          <%# Desktop only. Below md the engine navbar's phone row draws the
              theme toggle, so a second one here put two on every phone. The
              signed-out bar has always done it this way (layouts/_navbar). %>
          <span class="hidden md:flex" data-nav-theme-toggle="desktop"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <% div2_content = studio_nav_slot.call(div2_slot, div2_html) %>
      <% server_level = current_user.respond_to?(:level) && current_user.level.present? ? current_user.level : nil %>
      <% wallet_connected = current_user.respond_to?(:truncated_solana) && current_user.try(:solana_connected?) %>
      <% if div2_content.present? %>
        <%# Div 2 replaced by the consumer's slot (div2_slot or legacy div2_html). %>
        <%= div2_content %>
      <% elsif server_level || wallet_connected || show_logout_link %>
        <%# Div 2 (Smaller): wallet address (left) + level (right) with progress
            bar. Renders only when it has something to show — an off-chain,
            level-less user without a logout link gets NO second row, so the
            nav collapses to one line instead of an empty progress strip. %>
        <div x-data="{
               barWidth: 0,
               displayLevel: <%= server_level || 1 %>,
               leveledUp: false,
               init() {
                 var self = this;
                 var data = this.getSeedsData();
                 if (data) {
                   self.displayLevel = data.level;
                   setTimeout(function() { self.barWidth = data.progress; }, 150);
                 }
               },
               getSeedsData() {
                 try {
                   var raw = localStorage.getItem('seedsNavbar');
                   if (!raw) return null;
                   return JSON.parse(raw);
                 } catch(e) { return null; }
               },
               replayLevel() {
                 var self = this;
                 var data = this.getSeedsData();
                 var finalPct = data ? data.progress : self.barWidth;
                 self.displayLevel = Math.max(1, self.displayLevel - 1);
                 self.barWidth = 60;
                 setTimeout(function() { self.barWidth = 100; }, 300);
                 setTimeout(function() { self.displayLevel += 1; self.leveledUp = true; }, 1500);
                 setTimeout(function() { self.leveledUp = false; self.barWidth = 0; }, 2800);
                 setTimeout(function() { self.barWidth = finalPct; }, 3000);
               },
               handleSeedsUpdate(d) {
                 var self = this;
                 if (d.levelUp) {
                   self.barWidth = d.oldPct;
                   setTimeout(function() { self.barWidth = 100; }, 300);
                   setTimeout(function() { self.displayLevel = d.newLevel; self.leveledUp = true; }, 1500);
                   setTimeout(function() { self.leveledUp = false; self.barWidth = 0; }, 2800);
                   setTimeout(function() { self.barWidth = d.progress; }, 3000);
                 } else {
                   self.displayLevel = d.level;
                   self.barWidth = d.progress;
                 }
               }
             }"
             @navbar-replay-level.window="replayLevel()"
             @navbar-seeds-update.window="handleSeedsUpdate($event.detail)"
             class="relative mt-0.5" style="height: 14px;">
          <%# Fill bar %>
          <div class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 rounded z-0" style="background: var(--color-cta); transition: width 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);" :style="{ width: barWidth + '%' }"></div>
          <%# Text layer 1: muted (visible outside bar) %>
          <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-between px-1.5 font-mono text-muted z-[1] nav-bar-text">
            <span>
              <% if wallet_connected %>
                <%= current_user.truncated_solana %>
              <% end %>
            </span>
            <% if server_level %>
              <span :class="leveledUp && 'nav-level-pop'" x-text="'Level ' + displayLevel">Level <%= server_level %></span>
            <% elsif show_logout_link %>
              <%= link_to "Log out", logout_path, class: "font-mono text-muted no-underline nav-bar-text" %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <%# Text layer 2: white (clip-path reveals where bar covers) %>
          <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-between px-1.5 font-mono text-white z-[2] nav-bar-text" :style="{ 'clip-path': 'inset(0 ' + (100 - barWidth) + '% 0 0)' }">
            <span>
              <% if wallet_connected %>
                <%= current_user.truncated_solana %>
              <% end %>
            </span>
            <% if server_level %>
              <span :class="leveledUp && 'nav-level-pop'" x-text="'Level ' + displayLevel">Level <%= server_level %></span>
            <% elsif show_logout_link %>
              <%= link_to "Log out", logout_path, class: "font-mono text-white no-underline nav-bar-text" %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <style>
          @keyframes navLevelPop {
            0% { transform: scale(1); }
            15% { transform: scale(1.5); }
            35% { transform: scale(1.2); }
            50% { transform: scale(1.4); }
            70% { transform: scale(1.1); }
            100% { transform: scale(1); }
          }
          .nav-level-pop { animation: navLevelPop 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1); }
          .nav-bar-text { font-size: 10px; }
        </style>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%# Div 3 (Account): the name and the avatar are ONE link to the account
        page, one tab stop — they used to be two links to the same place.
        Below md the name is screen-reader text and the avatar stands alone,
        so a phone never shows the name truncated to "Guest 55…"; from md up
        it shows beside the avatar and truncates when the row is tight.

        The link is the nav root's shrinking flex item, so min-w-0 sits on it
        (a flex item defaults to min-width auto and would refuse to shrink),
        and again on the name's box, which is the link's own flex item. The
        avatar is aria-hidden: the name is the link's accessible name. %>
    <% account_classes = "group flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0 flex-shrink" %>
    <% account_inner = capture do %>
      <span class="sr-only md:not-sr-only md:min-w-0"><span class="block truncate text-right text-heading font-semibold text-base leading-none transition<%= " group-hover:text-primary" if studio_nav_destination %>" data-nav-name><%= current_user.display_name %></span></span>
      <span class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center" aria-hidden="true">
        <%= render "components/avatar", user: current_user, size: "nav" %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    <% if studio_nav_destination %>
      <%= link_to account_inner, studio_nav_destination, class: "#{account_classes} hover:opacity-80 transition", "data-nav-account": "", "x-bind:style": "$store.devMode && 'background: lightgreen'" %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="<%= account_classes %>" data-nav-account x-bind:style="$store.devMode && 'background: lightgreen'"><%= account_inner %></span>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render "components/admin_dropdown" unless respond_to?(:studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu?) && studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu? %>
    <%# Desktop only, as above: the phone row carries the toggle below md. %>
    <span class="hidden md:flex" data-nav-theme-toggle="desktop"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 ml-auto">
      <%= link_to "Log in", login_path, class: "text-heading hover:text-primary text-sm font-semibold transition" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign up", signup_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
